{"title":"João Renato Leripio","markdown":{"yaml":{"title":"","format":{"html":{"css":"cv_styles.css","toc":true,"toc-depth":2,"page-layout":"full","include-in-header":{"text":"<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.5.1/css/all.min.css\">\n"}}},"execute":{"echo":false}},"headingText":"João Renato Leripio","containsRefs":false,"markdown":"\n\n::: {.cv}\n\n::: {.header}\n\n\n::: {.subtitle}\nData, Modeling & Research Engineering\n:::\n\n::: {.contact}\n\n<span><i class=\"fa-solid fa-envelope\"></i> [joao@rleripio.com](mailto:joao@rleripio.com)</span>\n\n<span><i class=\"fa-brands fa-linkedin\"></i>[leripiorenato](https://www.linkedin.com/in/leripiorenato/)</span>\n\n<span><i class=\"fa-brands fa-github\"></i> [leripio](https://github.com/leripio)</span>\n\n<span><i class=\"fa-solid fa-globe\"></i> [rleripio.com](https://www.rleripio.com)</span>\n:::\n\n:::\n\n## Profile\n\nQuantitative researcher specializing in statistical modeling, forecasting, data products, and research engineering.\n\nExperienced in building end-to-end analytical workflows that transform raw data into models, analytical tools, and production-ready research outputs.\n\n## Professional Experience\n\n::: {.entry}\n::: {.entry-header}\n::: {.entry-title}\n### Kapitalo Investimentos\n\n**Data Science & Economic Modeling Lead**\n:::\n\n::: {.meta}\nSão Paulo, Brazil · 2022 - Present\n:::\n:::\n- Lead the Data Science and Modeling team within the Macroeconomic Research department, providing technical leadership and advancing the use of modern data and analytical technologies across research workflows.\n- Develop quantitative models and forecasting systems for macroeconomic analysis.\n- Build and maintain production analytical infrastructure, including data pipelines, automated reporting, and internal research applications.\n\n:::\n\n::: {.entry}\n::: {.entry-header}\n::: {.entry-title}\n### Itaú Asset Management\n\n**Quantitative Research Analyst**\n:::\n\n::: {.meta}\nSão Paulo, Brazil · 2019 - 2022\n:::\n:::\n\n- Developed quantitative models and forecasting tools for macroeconomic and financial analysis.\n- Integrated alternative datasets into investment research workflows.\n:::\n\n::: {.entry}\n::: {.entry-header}\n::: {.entry-title}\n### IPEDF\n\n**Economic Research Analyst**\n:::\n\n::: {.meta}\nBrasília, Brazil · 2017 - 2019\n:::\n:::\n\n- Conducted regional economic analysis and monitoring of economic activity indicators.\n- Produced reports and studies supporting public policy discussions and decision-making.\n- Developed statistical indicators and analytical tools for economic assessment.\n:::\n\n## Education\n\n**M.S. in Economics**, Universidade Federal Fluminense · 2017  \n**B.S. in Economics**, Universidade Federal Fluminense · 2013\n\n## Publications\n\nAuthor of [*R for Economic Research*](http://book.rleripio.com), a practical guide to data analysis, statistical modeling, and forecasting for applied research.\n\n## Selected Presentations\n\n- **Nowcasting when predictors keep changing. Leveraging cross-sectional information in high-dimensional, high-turnover data** - International Symposium on Forecasting · Montreal · 2026\n\n- **Nowcasting Inflation in Brazil Using Web Data** - International Symposium on Forecasting · Charlottesville · 2023\n\n- **Real-time Forecasting COVID-19 Cases Applied to US Regions** - International Symposium on Forecasting · Remote · 2020\n:::","srcMarkdownNoYaml":"\n\n::: {.cv}\n\n::: {.header}\n\n# João Renato Leripio\n\n::: {.subtitle}\nData, Modeling & Research Engineering\n:::\n\n::: {.contact}\n\n<span><i class=\"fa-solid fa-envelope\"></i> [joao@rleripio.com](mailto:joao@rleripio.com)</span>\n\n<span><i class=\"fa-brands fa-linkedin\"></i>[leripiorenato](https://www.linkedin.com/in/leripiorenato/)</span>\n\n<span><i class=\"fa-brands fa-github\"></i> [leripio](https://github.com/leripio)</span>\n\n<span><i class=\"fa-solid fa-globe\"></i> [rleripio.com](https://www.rleripio.com)</span>\n:::\n\n:::\n\n## Profile\n\nQuantitative researcher specializing in statistical modeling, forecasting, data products, and research engineering.\n\nExperienced in building end-to-end analytical workflows that transform raw data into models, analytical tools, and production-ready research outputs.\n\n## Professional Experience\n\n::: {.entry}\n::: {.entry-header}\n::: {.entry-title}\n### Kapitalo Investimentos\n\n**Data Science & Economic Modeling Lead**\n:::\n\n::: {.meta}\nSão Paulo, Brazil · 2022 - Present\n:::\n:::\n- Lead the Data Science and Modeling team within the Macroeconomic Research department, providing technical leadership and advancing the use of modern data and analytical technologies across research workflows.\n- Develop quantitative models and forecasting systems for macroeconomic analysis.\n- Build and maintain production analytical infrastructure, including data pipelines, automated reporting, and internal research applications.\n\n:::\n\n::: {.entry}\n::: {.entry-header}\n::: {.entry-title}\n### Itaú Asset Management\n\n**Quantitative Research Analyst**\n:::\n\n::: {.meta}\nSão Paulo, Brazil · 2019 - 2022\n:::\n:::\n\n- Developed quantitative models and forecasting tools for macroeconomic and financial analysis.\n- Integrated alternative datasets into investment research workflows.\n:::\n\n::: {.entry}\n::: {.entry-header}\n::: {.entry-title}\n### IPEDF\n\n**Economic Research Analyst**\n:::\n\n::: {.meta}\nBrasília, Brazil · 2017 - 2019\n:::\n:::\n\n- Conducted regional economic analysis and monitoring of economic activity indicators.\n- Produced reports and studies supporting public policy discussions and decision-making.\n- Developed statistical indicators and analytical tools for economic assessment.\n:::\n\n## Education\n\n**M.S. in Economics**, Universidade Federal Fluminense · 2017  \n**B.S. in Economics**, Universidade Federal Fluminense · 2013\n\n## Publications\n\nAuthor of [*R for Economic Research*](http://book.rleripio.com), a practical guide to data analysis, statistical modeling, and forecasting for applied research.\n\n## Selected Presentations\n\n- **Nowcasting when predictors keep changing. Leveraging cross-sectional information in high-dimensional, high-turnover data** - International Symposium on Forecasting · Montreal · 2026\n\n- **Nowcasting Inflation in Brazil Using Web Data** - International Symposium on Forecasting · Charlottesville · 2023\n\n- **Real-time Forecasting COVID-19 Cases Applied to US Regions** - International Symposium on Forecasting · Remote · 2020\n:::"},"formats":{"html":{"identifier":{"display-name":"HTML","target-format":"html","base-format":"html"},"execute":{"fig-width":7,"fig-height":5,"fig-format":"retina","fig-dpi":96,"df-print":"default","error":false,"eval":true,"cache":null,"freeze":false,"echo":false,"output":true,"warning":true,"include":true,"keep-md":false,"keep-ipynb":false,"ipynb":null,"enabled":null,"daemon":null,"daemon-restart":false,"debug":false,"ipynb-filters":[],"ipynb-shell-interactivity":null,"plotly-connected":true,"engine":"markdown"},"render":{"keep-tex":false,"keep-typ":false,"keep-source":false,"keep-hidden":false,"prefer-html":false,"output-divs":true,"output-ext":"html","fig-align":"default","fig-pos":null,"fig-env":null,"code-fold":"none","code-overflow":"scroll","code-link":false,"code-line-numbers":false,"code-tools":false,"tbl-colwidths":"auto","merge-includes":true,"inline-includes":false,"preserve-yaml":false,"latex-auto-mk":true,"latex-auto-install":true,"latex-clean":true,"latex-min-runs":1,"latex-max-runs":10,"latex-makeindex":"makeindex","latex-makeindex-opts":[],"latex-tlmgr-opts":[],"latex-input-paths":[],"latex-output-dir":null,"link-external-icon":false,"link-external-newwindow":false,"self-contained-math":false,"format-resources":[],"notebook-links":true},"pandoc":{"standalone":true,"wrap":"none","default-image-extension":"png","to":"html","toc":true,"css":["cv_styles.css"],"toc-depth":2,"include-in-head